  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Bond strength is inversely proportional to the bond length of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>&nbsp;bond of hydrides of 16th group hydrides. The bond length increases down the group. Hence, bond dissociation enthalpy decreases down the group.</p><p>Hence, bond dissociation energy of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> bond in hydrides of group 16 follows the order</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>Se</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>Te</mi></math>.</p>",
